{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSWdqfnpx3jYhPdFmZBm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Requirement, restated:** Add an HTTP POST endpoint at `/shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that transitions a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status, is idempotent (retries on `CONFIRMED` succeed without change), rejects `CANCELLED` shipments with HTTP 409, and rejects non-existent shipments with HTTP 404.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment domain: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27` - data class with status field; enum has CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- Controller: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56` - @RestController with create/getById/list\n- Repository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` - InMemoryShipmentRepository with save/findById/existsById\n- Error handling: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` - ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- Error codes: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` - machine-readable closed set\n- Exception handler: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-29` - converts ApiException to ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw domain exceptions; GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError envelope with machine-readable code\n- 201 (CREATED) for POST that creates, 200 (OK) for successful operations, 404 for not found, 409 for state conflicts\n- Repository pattern with in-memory backing\n- Tests use MockMvc with status().isNotFound, status().isConflict, jsonPath assertions on error.code\n- Error messages are human-readable prose; codes are machine-readable\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` — must add ErrorCode for \"shipment cannot be confirmed in current state\" (409 case)\n2. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` — must add confirm endpoint with status 200\n3. `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for all four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- New ErrorCode is part of the public API contract; must be deliberately chosen\n- Idempotency: CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED must not change status, or retries fail\n- Immutability: Shipment is a data class; updating requires new instance via `copy()`\n- Existing tests must not break; new tests must add coverage without modifying test structure\n\n**Open questions:**\nThe ticket does not name an ErrorCode for the 409 case. I will use `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRMATION` to follow the existing naming pattern (SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS). No ambiguity remains; all four cases are well-defined.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRMATION` to the ErrorCode enum. This signals that the shipment is in a state that does not permit confirmation (specifically, CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Takes `shipmentId` from path variable\n   - Fetches the shipment via repository; throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with the new error code (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, update the shipment's status to CONFIRMED and persist it\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - Return the shipment (unchanged if already confirmed) with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and moves it to CONFIRMED` — create S-1, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED\n   - `confirming an already confirmed shipment succeeds without change` — create, confirm, confirm again, verify still CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409 and error envelope` — manually write a CANCELLED shipment to repository, attempt confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRMATION code\n   - `rejects confirming a nonexistent shipment with 404` — attempt confirm on S-missing, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n- **Alternative 1: Add a separate service layer** — Not needed. The existing controller handles the logic directly and the repository is trivial. Adding a service adds layers without benefit in this simple case.\n- **Alternative 2: Use a different error code like SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM** — Considered but SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRMATION is more explicit about why: the state (CANCELLED) is invalid for this operation. Consistent with \"state\" language in the enum.\n- **Alternative 3: Add a new exception type** — Not needed. ConflictException already means \"request conflicts with current state\" which is exactly what happens when trying to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Reads | Writes | Flow | Response |\n|------|-------|--------|------|----------|\n| CREATED shipment | repository.findById() | repository.save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | Happy path | 200 OK with updated Shipment |\n| Already CONFIRMED | repository.findById() | (nothing) | Idempotent no-op | 200 OK with unchanged Shipment |\n| CANCELLED | repository.findById() → throw ConflictException | (none) | Exception caught by GlobalExceptionHandler | 409 with ApiError envelope, code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRMATION |\n| Not found | repository.findById() returns null → throw ResourceNotFoundException | (none) | Exception caught by GlobalExceptionHandler | 404 with ApiError envelope, code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: confirms a created shipment** — Create S-1 with POST /shipments, POST /shipments/S-1/confirm, verify 200 and status is CONFIRMED. Checks the happy path (CREATED→CONFIRMED).\n\n2. **Test: idempotent confirm** — Create S-2, POST confirm twice, verify both return 200 and second returns same unchanged shipment. Checks retry safety.\n\n3. **Test: reject cancelled shipment** — Directly add a CANCELLED shipment to repository (no endpoint creates one), POST confirm, verify 409 and error.code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRMATION. Checks the conflict case.\n\n4. **Test: reject unknown id** — POST confirm on S-unknown without creating it, verify 404 and error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND. Checks the not-found case.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Starting with the ErrorCode enum:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2212,"cache_read_input_tokens":18252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2212},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e6badf2-ca00-44a9-ab9a-605c8a50701c","uuid":"2b438dc6-3530-4926-86ae-04d58bb177a5","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:19:22.478Z","request_id":"req_011CfSWdqD1nM83PCHVz5uBg"}
